    "type": "question",
    "label": "18",
    "prompt": "A 250 mL packet of milk contains 295 mg calcium and 110 mg of phosphorus. Give the ratio of calcium to phosphorus in simplest form.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$59:22$",
      "worked": "The highest common factor of 295 and 110 is 5.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{calcium}:\\text{phosphorus}&=295:110\\\\\\text{calcium}:\\text{phosphorus}&=(295\\div5):(110\\div5)\\\\\\text{calcium}:\\text{phosphorus}&=59:22\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
